1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,835
Ostwald's dilution law.

2
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:06,341
Take a weak electrolyte A B at concentration C.

3
00:00:06,341 --> 00:00:13,111
At equilibrium, a fraction alpha, the degree of ionisation, has split into ions.

4
00:00:13,111 --> 00:00:19,986
So the ions are C alpha each, and the molecules left are C times one minus alpha.

